  "bio_summary": "Narain Karthikeyan is an Indian racing driver who made history as the first Indian to compete in Formula One, debuting in 2005. Throughout his career, he has competed in various international racing series including A1GP, Le Mans Series, NASCAR, Super Formula, and Super GT. He achieved his best Formula One result with a 4th place finish at the 2005 United States Grand Prix. Karthikeyan continues to be involved in motorsport, currently serving as Mentor and Head of Driver Development for Ajith Racing and competing in the Asian Le Mans Series in 2026.",
